mcu_step: decide the fixed per-instruction work once

MCU_Step() runs twice per emulated instruction pair of tests that can only have
one answer for a given romset, and makes one call that almost always does
nothing:

  * `!is_mk1 && !is_jv880 && !is_scb55` -- three loads and three branches to
    re-derive a fact fixed when the romset is set.  MCU_SetRomset() is the only
    place any of those flags changes, so it computes has_submcu there instead.

  * MCU_UpdateAnalog()'s entire body is under `if (ctrl & 0x20)`; its else
    branch is a single store of 0 to analog_end_time.  Testing the bit at the
    call site keeps the call out of the common path.  This is outlining a cold
    path, not reordering branches by frequency -- the bit is read either way.

Measured (callgrind Ir, mk2, 32 PCM slots, placeholder ROMs), on top of 0001:
7,836,682,972 -> 7,761,848,566, -0.96%; 11.7 instructions per emulated
instruction.

Proof: patches/tests/mcu_step_fixed_work_equivalence.cpp.

--- a/src/backend/mcu.h
+++ b/src/backend/mcu.h
@@ -274,6 +274,11 @@
     bool is_scb55 = false; // 0 - sub mcu (e.g SC-55mk2), 1 - no sub mcu (e.g SCB-55)
     bool is_sc155 = false; // 0 - SC-55(MK2), 1 - SC-155(MK2)
 
+    // Derived from the flags above by MCU_SetRomset(), which is the only place
+    // any of them changes. True when this romset has a sub-MCU that MCU_Step()
+    // has to clock; false when it drives the dummy UART instead.
+    bool has_submcu = true;
+
     uint32_t rom2_mask = ROM2_SIZE - 1;
 
     bool ga_int[8]{};
--- a/src/backend/mcu.cpp
+++ b/src/backend/mcu.cpp
@@ -926,7 +926,8 @@
 
     TIMER_Clock(*mcu.timer, mcu.cycles);
 
-    if (!mcu.is_mk1 && !mcu.is_jv880 && !mcu.is_scb55)
+    // has_submcu is the same predicate, decided once when the romset is set.
+    if (mcu.has_submcu)
         SM_Update(*mcu.sm, mcu.cycles);
     else
     {
@@ -934,7 +935,13 @@
         MCU_UpdateUART_TX(mcu);
     }
 
-    MCU_UpdateAnalog(mcu, mcu.cycles);
+    // MCU_UpdateAnalog()'s whole body is under `if (ctrl & 0x20)`, and its else
+    // branch is this one store. Testing here keeps the call out of the common
+    // path; see patches/tests/mcu_step_fixed_work_equivalence.cpp.
+    if (mcu.dev_register[DEV_ADCSR] & 0x20)
+        MCU_UpdateAnalog(mcu, mcu.cycles);
+    else
+        mcu.analog_end_time = 0;
 
     if (mcu.is_mk1)
     {
@@ -1056,5 +1063,7 @@
         break;
     }
 
+    mcu.has_submcu = !mcu.is_mk1 && !mcu.is_jv880 && !mcu.is_scb55;
+
     TIMER_NotifyRomsetChange(*mcu.timer);
 }
